private static final int[][] DIRECTIONS = {{0, 1}, {1, 0}, {0, -1}, {-1, 0}};

public static int countOilDeposits(char[][] grid) {
    int count = 0;
    int rows = grid.length;
    int cols = grid[0].length;

    for (int i = 0; i < rows; i++) {
        for (int j = 0; j < cols; j++) {
            if (grid[i][j] == '@') {
                DFS(grid, i, j, count);
            }
        }
    }
    return count;
}

private static void DFS(char[][] grid, int i, int j, int count) {
    if (i < 0 || i >= grid.length || j < 0 || j >= grid[0].length || grid[i][j] != '@') {
        return;
    }
    grid[i][j] = '*'; // Mark as visited
    count++;

    for (int[] direction : DIRECTIONS) {
        DFS(grid, i + direction[0], j + direction[1], count);
    }
}
```
The `countOilDeposits` function initializes a counter and iterates through each cell in the grid. If a cell contains an oil pocket ('@'), it calls the `DFS` function to traverse the connected components of oil deposits and increase the counter. The `DFS` function marks each visited cell as '*' to avoid revisiting and continuously explores its connected components.

